tion.\n\nWhich should I roll back?\n1. **`payments-api` \u2192 v5.0.0**\n2. **`payments-worker` \u2192 v3.3.0**\n3. **Both.** With identical error rates, one failure may be causing the other, or both releases may be bad.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll do the rollback and open the SEV2 incident for that service, or one per service if it's both. Both targets were healthy in production before, so no change-manager approval is needed. There are no open incidents yet, so this won't duplicate a page.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EPua7sBK4Le53iB2qHQc9k", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MyL1CzqZMdB7v8g41RvsvK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 errors after deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "This morning's payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy is unhealthy, with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at 18%, which is believed to be downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last healthy production release. Watch payments-api recovery after the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01K5kpWgQmhsiX4CC2BARizr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NJniMQR7Ax4MaGibz3urqo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2 incident. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still failing.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is back on v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. That's done in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%, and it now shows as healthy.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 against payments-worker, and on-call has been paged. The summary notes the effect on payments-api.\n- **payments-api:** it's still on v5.1.0 and its error rate is still 18%. It may just not have caught up yet, but the unchanged rate could also mean v5.1.0 has its own problem, separate from the worker.\n\nI left payments-api alone since you said its errors come from the worker. Give it a few minutes. If its error rate doesn't come down, I'd suggest rolling it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release; just tell me to go ahead. If that happens, I'll also add payments-api to INC-0001.", "type": "text"}]}]}